# ============================================================================
# MORROWMERE CITY  (twin city, 30x22 blocks, buffer 1008/1300)  johto_modern
# ============================================================================
# HOOK: "the city of yesterday and tomorrow". The wide River Mere splits it
#   into YESTERSIDE (west: the old castle-town of brown-roof houses, the
#   Gym, museum and inn) and MORROWSIDE (east: glass towers, the Magnet
#   Train terminus, the Grand Hotel). The two wards bicker about everything
#   except the Clock Tower on Hourglass Isle mid-river, which keeps time
#   for both. The clock has stopped; each ward blames the other, the island
#   is closed, and the Gym leader (a clockmaker) is stuck up the tower.
#   Suggested Gym type: STEEL (clockwork) or PSYCHIC (time).
#   Unlike Silkwater's railed canals, the Mere is one wide natural river
#   with 58/59 shores, edge to edge, and a quayed island in the middle.
#
# DISTRICTS / BUILDINGS (door steps in exit lines)
#   Yesterside (cols 0-9)
#     Morrowmere Gym (4x2, NW)          - leader up the tower until beat 4
#     Clockmaker's (brown 2x2)          - repairs; gives a Metal Coat/TM later
#     Lantern Inn (3x2)                 - old cheap inn: rest + PC box
#     Tea House (brown 2x2)             - rumours, a daily berry-tea heal item
#     Guildhall (3x2)                   - old-ward council; key NPC for beat 2
#     Yesterday Museum (3x2, 1a door)   - fossils / old Johto history
#     Antiques (brown 2x2)              - sells evolution stones, rotating stock
#     Ferryman (3x2)                    - river tour / Surf hint; owns the pier
#     3 homes; Hour Garden (headbutt trees, hidden item); Old Main St
#     (brick, W exit); riverside promenade (brick, col 9) with planters
#   The River Mere (cols 10-19)
#     Old Bridge (rows 4-5): full-width railed bridge carrying Main St
#     Hourglass Isle: fenced stone quay, CLOCK TOWER (spire + radio-tower
#       art, door on the island plaza); two short bridges W and E (rows 15-16)
#     Fishing pier off Yesterside (rows 19-20); rocks + hidden items by Surf
#   Morrowside (cols 20-29)
#     Magnet Train Station (3x2, NE) with fenced tracks running off E edge
#     Morrow Tower (silver 2x3)         - tech firm HQ, beat 3 dungeon
#     Grand Hotel (4x4 window tower)    - pricey hotel: rest + PC box + concierge
#     Link Center (3x3, PCC art)        - trades / link battles (not a PkMn Ctr)
#     Mart (2x2), Studio tower (silver 2x3, TV/radio studio)
#     Riverside Apartments W/E (3x2 each); Skyline Park lawns (S)
#
# GAMEPLAY BEATS
#   1. Arrive from the W (Old Main St) or by Magnet Train into the Station.
#   2. Gym locked; workers bar both island bridges ("clock stopped, isle
#      closed"). The Guildhall blames Morrowside, the Grand Hotel concierge
#      blames Yesterside.
#   3. Morrowside: Morrow Tower's lab "borrowed" the clock's mainspring for
#      a prototype -- short tower dungeon (Rocket-style grunts or a rogue
#      scientist), recover the spring.
#   4. Clockmaker fits it; workers step aside. Clock Tower interior: gear /
#      pendulum floors, the Gym leader at the top battles you as a warm-up
#      and the clock restarts (time-of-day events resume, night palette:
#      lit windows across Morrowside, lanterns in Yesterside).
#   5. Gym opens. Post-Surf: river N/S routes, pier fishing, river rocks.
#
# EXITS / CONNECTIONS
#   W  rows 4-5   Old Main St -> route west
#   E  rows 4-5   Morrow Avenue -> route east
#   S  cols 24-25 Skyline Park avenue -> route south
#   River N/S edges (cols 11-18): Surf connections up/down the Mere
#   Magnet Train from the Station (warp, not an edge)
#
# TILE GAPS / UNCERTAIN BLOCKS
#   - No bridge deck art: bridges are 41 over 49 pavement with rails.
#   - No bottom-shore water piece, so the river runs edge to edge and the
#     island is a fenced quay (40-4a) instead of a natural island.
#   - Clock face: the 21 spire's dish reads as a clock; a real clock-face
#     block would sell the landmark better.
#   - The 2f "trees" on the island/garden are headbutt shrubs on grass.
#   - Link Center uses the 5f "PCC" sign; reword or redraw if unwanted.
#   - 0f in the Grand Hotel's bottom row (A D F Z) is a plain wall filler.
# ============================================================================
tileset johto_modern
ref GoldenrodCity
key T=05 .=01 :=06 ,=02 *=04 h=67 o=0a
key [=58 ~=35 ]=59 %=34 $=36
key f=41 e=49 r=40 t=42 l=48 j=4a <=44 >=46 s=45 S=77 w=66 x=80 z=81
key R=18 M=1f N=19 A=10 D=17 Z=11 E=1a F=0f C=1c Q=1d W=1e O=16 K=33 H=27 I=23 J=28 1=14 2=13 3=12 5=64 9=08 0=09 b=2b c=2c
key i=25 k=26 y=29 q=2a d=2d m=2e g=21 G=22 X=20 Y=24 V=5f
key _=7e #=7f @=2f !=3b &=3f
grid:
TRMMNT90hT[~~~~~~~~]TRMNTTTTTT
TCFQW.OW.:[~~%~~~~~]:EFZ______
T........:[~~~~~$~~]::::ffffff
